<Layout title="Kaspersky — Nikita Ostroukhov" description="Nikita Ostroukhov’s work at Kaspersky.">
  <header><h1>Kaspersky</h1><p class="subtitle">Identity and access management and incident response systems.</p></header>
  <section>
    <p>
      From 2021 to 2022, I worked at <a href="https://kaspersky.ru/">Kaspersky</a> as a Senior Software Engineer,
      developing internal infrastructure for identity and access management
      and incident response automation.
    </p>
    <p>
      I joined with several years of production Go experience at a time when
      Go adoption within the company was still relatively early, and contributed
      to establishing engineering practices around the language alongside my
      product work.
    </p>
    <p>
      My work focused on two systems: an in-house <a href="https://support.kaspersky.ru/ksc/15.1/221048">IAM</a> platform based on OAuth 2.0
      and OpenID Connect, and an incident response platform built around Temporal
      workflow orchestration.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="contributions">
    <h2>Selected work</h2>
    <p>
      <span class="contribution-title">Identity and Access Management</span><br />
      <span class="contribution-details">→ Designed and implemented Kaspersky’s in-house IAM system, partially based on a fork of ORY Hydra, with substantial protocol modifications while remaining compliant with OAuth 2.0 and OpenID Connect.</span>
    </p>
    <p>
      <span class="contribution-title">Incident Response</span><br />
      <span class="contribution-details">→ Developed an incident response platform based on Temporal workflow orchestration, including a custom-designed DSL for defining and executing response workflows.</span>
    </p>
    <p>
      <span class="contribution-title">Go Engineering Practices</span><br />
      <span class="contribution-details">→ Helped establish Go engineering practices within the company, including coding standards, interview tasks, shared internal libraries, and development conventions.</span>
    </p>
  </section>

